{"id":107237987564206,"type":"album","name":"The Long Run","artist":"Eagles","year":1979,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://coverartarchive.org/release-group/1a265de4-136d-3414-adf5-b0913ca2aa15/front-500","yt":"kQ9-HIi5kB0","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/eagles/the-long-run"}},"artist_ref":{"id":106115726467187,"name":"The Eagles","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/178be204025c8d38a72113564b647baf/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":133646791193319,"type":"genre","name":"Laurel Canyon Scene","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":200,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":177455037556203,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements — Laurel Canyon Scene","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":197,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album was the much-anticipated follow-up to \"Hotel California.\" The band's cover of \"Please Come Home for Christmas\" and the original B-side \"Funky New Year\" were recorded to appease the record label and break up monotony while \"The Long Run\" was still in production, helping to keep the label patient until its release in 1979. \"It did the trick of keeping a silent record at bay until the long run was released in 1979.\"","year":1979,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 52 - 70s Christmas Music","url":null}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album was widely believed to be the band's final record at the time of its release. Critics often did not love \"The Long Run\" or even the Eagles themselves, frequently perceiving them as \"too corporate.\" \"It's the final track on what we thought was going to be the last Eagles album. Of course, that was a long run.\"","year":1979,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 41 - The Impact of The Troubadour on 1970s Popular Culture","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/ep-41-the-impact-of-the-troubadour-on-1970s-popular-culture"},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 41 - The Impact of The Troubadour on 1970s Popular Culture","url":null}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":147132100610675,"type":"album","name":"Hotel California","year":1976,"weight":38},{"id":176138389135991,"type":"song","name":"One of These Nights","year":1975,"weight":28},{"id":170101285485673,"type":"album","name":"Desperado","year":1972,"weight":28},{"id":174811107218091,"type":"album","name":"One of These Nights","year":1975,"weight":23},{"id":135134731009764,"type":"song","name":"Lyin' Eyes","year":1976,"weight":21},{"id":59847593244658,"type":"album","name":"Eagles","year":1972,"weight":20},{"id":117234253472183,"type":"song","name":"Hotel California","year":1977,"weight":17},{"id":55222976077620,"type":"album","name":"On the Border","year":1974,"weight":16},{"id":26937411688903,"type":"song","name":"Take It to the Limit","year":1976,"weight":14},{"id":280136024106097,"type":"song","name":"Old 55","year":1974,"weight":10},{"id":273853926658019,"type":"song","name":"You Can Close Your Eyes","year":null,"weight":10},{"id":266010762320488,"type":"song","name":"Take It Easy","year":1972,"weight":10}]}